bbs — provenance note
======================

Kept as a module-local NOTICE (same placement as the sibling `bls12_381`/
`frost`/`voprf`/`bulletproofs`/`bn254` modules — self-contained crypto
modules not folded into the root `NOTICE`).

Provenance
----------

bbs — the protocol design follows **draft-irtf-cfrg-bbs-signatures-04**
(fetched 2026-07-16 from `https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/
draft-irtf-cfrg-bbs-signatures-04.txt`), the BLS12-381-SHA-256
ciphersuite (§6.2.2). This is a public IETF Internet-Draft; the draft's
TEXT (the protocol description/equations being followed) is not itself
a copyrightable implementation, and no source code accompanying the
draft was consulted or ported — see CONVENTIONS.md §5's merger-doctrine
note (the same posture this repo's other spec-derived modules take for
their own IETF sources).

**Why draft-04, not the current draft (`-10` as of this writing)**: the
BBS Signatures draft's CoreSign/ProofGen wire format changed across
revisions (confirmed at drafts `-06` and `-05` respectively — see
`SPEC.md`'s version-pinning section for the byte-level evidence), and
this module's KAT vectors are drawn from a reference implementation
whose fixtures happen to match draft-04, not the current draft. See
`SPEC.md` for the full determination methodology.

